## Overview

Fixes two `lfm2` tool-parser bugs that together make LFM2.5 agents loop on the same tool call under `tool_choice="required"`:

1. Forced `tool_choice` (`required`/named) was decoded as a JSON tool-call list instead of LFM2's trained `<|tool_call_start|>[name(k=v)]<|tool_call_end|>` block. An `lfm2` structural tag now constrains it to the native block.
2. Tool names with hyphens (`sub-task-ending`) came back as content. They are now parsed.

Related: #57989 (the same hyphen fix for FunctionGemma).

## Claims

- On a [ToolSandbox](https://github.com/apple-aiml-research/ToolSandbox) turn where the search already succeeded, `LiquidAI/LFM2.5-2.6B` repeats it in 28/30 samples on `main` and ends the subtask in 30/30 with this PR.
- `required`/named calls are decoded in the native block and parsed by `Lfm2ToolParser`, like `auto`. `auto` is constrained only when a structural tag applies anyway (a `strict` tool, `--tool-strict-level`, `parallel_tool_calls=false`), and plain text stays valid.
- Hyphenated names parse in streaming and non-streaming, including parallel blocks that mix them with plain names.

## Validation

**Reproducer.** ToolSandbox's contacts task with `tool_choice="required"`, at the turn after a successful `search_contacts(relationship="friend")`. The harness adds a `sub-task-ending` tool, which is the correct next call.

```bash
vllm serve LiquidAI/LFM2.5-2.6B --enable-auto-tool-choice --tool-call-parser lfm2 --reasoning-parser qwen3
curl -s localhost:8000/v1/chat/completions -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d @toolsandbox_repro.json \
  | jq -r '.choices[].message.tool_calls | map(.function.name) | join(",")' | sort | uniq -c
```

<details>
<summary><code>toolsandbox_repro.json</code> (the model's default sampling, <code>n=30</code>)</summary>

```json
{
  "model": "LiquidAI/LFM2.5-2.6B",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "system",
      "content": "Execute only the current subtask in the final user message. Earlier user/assistant pairs are completed prerequisites: the user message is the prerequisite objective and the assistant message is its final result. Use them only as context. Never attempt later subtasks.\n\nRules:\n- Use only exposed tools through API tool calls; never output plain text or textual tool-call JSON.\n- Call task tools as needed, including repeated calls, and wait for each response. Continue until the complete objective is satisfied.\n- Never fabricate, guess, or assume data. Use only user-message or tool-response values, even when another value seems obvious.\n- Include only needed optional arguments known from a user message or tool response. Omit unknown optional arguments; never use placeholders such as `0`, `\"\"`, or `null`.\n- Do not ask the user for credentials or task data; retrieve them with available tools.\n- Call `sub-task-ending` exactly once after task tools, or immediately if none are needed.\n\n`sub-task-ending` arguments:\n- Required top-level `status`: `Completed`, `UnknownError`, or `MissingRequiredInputOrTool`.\n- Required `data`: a non-empty string.\n- `Completed`: ONLY if every objective requirement was achieved. Failed, partial, or unverified outcomes are NEVER `Completed`, even when `data` explains them. Include all requested result values.\n- `MissingRequiredInputOrTool`: a required capability or information cannot be obtained; state what is missing in `data`.\n- `UnknownError`: an unexpected failure that may be corrected with available information and tools; describe it in `data`."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Search for all contacts to identify friends"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "id": "call_search",
          "type": "function",
          "function": {
            "name": "search_contacts",
            "arguments": "{\"relationship\": \"friend\"}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_search",
      "content": "{\"status\":\"ok\",\"tool\":\"search_contacts\",\"http_status\":200,\"response\":{\"tool_name\":\"search_contacts\",\"arguments\":{\"relationship\":\"friend\"},\"result\":[{\"person_id\":\"9e137f06-916a-5310-8174-cf0b7e9f7054\",\"name\":\"Fredrik Thordendal\",\"phone_number\":\"+12453344098\",\"relationship\":\"friend\",\"is_self\":false},{\"person_id\":\"a22e1984-6c6c-530c-8831-c3ea3b5138e7\",\"name\":\"John Petrucci\",\"phone_number\":\"+1234560987\",\"relationship\":\"friend\",\"is_self\":false}],\"tool_error\":null,\"tool_trace\":[]}}"
    }
  ],
  "tools": [
    {
      "type": "function",
      "function": {
        "name": "search_contacts",
        "description": "Search for a contact person based on provided arguments Each field has a search criteria of either\n1. Exact value matching\n2. Fuzzy string matching with a predefined threshold\nSearch results contains all contact entries that matched all criteria",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "person_id": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "String format unique identifier for the contact person, will be exact matched"
            },
            "name": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Name of contact person, will be fuzzy matched"
            },
            "phone_number": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Phone number of contact person, will be exact matched"
            },
            "relationship": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Relationship between user and this contact, will be fuzzy matched"
            },
            "is_self": {
              "type": "boolean",
              "description": "If the requested contact corresponds to the current user. Will be exact matched"
            }
          },
          "required": []
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "function",
      "function": {
        "name": "sub-task-ending",
        "description": "End the current executor subtask. Call this exactly once after the subtask has completed, failed unexpectedly, or cannot continue because a required capability or required information is unavailable.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "status": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "Completed",
                "UnknownError",
                "MissingRequiredInputOrTool"
              ],
              "description": "Required top-level subtask status. Use exactly one of Completed, UnknownError, or MissingRequiredInputOrTool."
            },
            "data": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Required non-empty text. For Completed include the complete result and every value requested by the objective. For failures describe the problem precisely."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "status",
            "data"
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "tool_choice": "required",
  "temperature": 0.1,
  "top_k": 50,
  "repetition_penalty": 1.1,
  "n": 30
}
```
</details>

| | `main` | this PR |
|---|---|---|
| curl above, 30 samples | `search_contacts` repeated in 28 | `sub-task-ending` in 30 |
| full agent loop, 10 runs × up to 8 turns | repeat loop in 7 | 0 |

**Tests.** `vllm/vllm-openai:latest` (v0.32.0) on an RTX 4070 (8 GB). E2E: `main`'s or this branch's two changed files copied over the installed ones. Unit: this branch's Python tree with the image's compiled extensions.

```
# before (main)
$ pytest tests/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/test_lfm2_tool_calls.py
E   AssertionError: assert [] == ['get-weather']
E   AssertionError: assert 124905 in [67, 266, 229, 206, 2718, 463, ...]   # no <|tool_call_start|>
4 failed

# after (this branch)
$ pytest tests/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/test_lfm2_tool_calls.py
4 passed
$ pytest tests/tool_parsers/test_lfm2_tool_parser.py tests/tool_parsers/test_structural_tag_registry.py
348 passed
```

New tests cover hyphenated names (parser), the `lfm2` grammar's accept/reject cases, the real token stream and a `DelegatingParser` round trip (registry), and an e2e test on `LFM2.5-2.6B` that runs in the existing `entrypoints/openai/chat_completion` CI step.

## Details

**Forced tool_choice.** `Lfm2ToolParser` had no `structural_tag_model`, so forced calls got the generic JSON schema and bypassed the parser. Outside its trained format the model copies its previous call: after `</think>`, the JSON prefix `[{"name": "` gives `search` 0.53 / `sub` 0.32 at the first token, while `<|tool_call_start|>[` gives `sub` 1.00. The fix registers `get_lfm2_structural_tag` (like `hermes`, `longcat` and `plamo3`; nothing shared changes): the start token, then `[` + an allowed name + `(`, then free text up to the end token. The sentinels are strings because request validation compiles the tag without a tokenizer, and the arguments use `AnyTextFormat` because LFM2 tokens such as `(city` span the forced prefix. `VLLM_ENFORCE_STRICT_TOOL_CALLING=0` restores the old behavior.

**Hyphenated names.** `ast.parse` reads `sub-task-ending(...)` as a subtraction. Requested names that aren't identifiers are swapped for `_lfm2_tool_alias_N` at call positions before parsing and restored afterwards. Names not in `request.tools` are left alone.

**Limitations.** Only the first call's name is constrained. Further calls and all arguments are free text, so arguments aren't checked against the schema, even for `strict` tools. `parallel_tool_calls=false` is enforced after parsing, not by the grammar.

**Docs.** New LFM2.5 section in `docs/features/tool_calling.md`. The LFM rows in `docs/models/supported_models.md` now list LFM2.5 checkpoints; the deprecated LFM2 and LFM2-VL examples are dropped.

**Not a duplicate.** No open upstream PR covers LFM2 tool calling or an `lfm2` structural tag. #52900 (Rust-frontend LFM2 parser) is unaffected.

